# Citation metadata. GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this
# file, and Zenodo reads it when archiving a release, so the DOI record carries
# these fields rather than whatever Zenodo can infer from the repository.
#
# Validate with: pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: ReadRift
abstract: >-
  Visualisation of assembly errors, prophage induction and genomic variation by
  re-mapping long sequence reads. ReadRift classifies every read by how its BLAST
  alignment divides - contiguously, or into pieces that map far apart, in
  opposite orientation, or onto a different contig - and draws the result as a
  wide multi-page map plus an interactive genome browser. Reads that divide are
  evidence of structural variation, inversions, transposition, phage excision or
  circularity.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/skovgaard-ole/readrift"
authors:
  - family-names: Skovgaard
    given-names: Ole
    email: olesk@ruc.dk
    affiliation: Roskilde University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4860-1847"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - long-read sequencing
  - nanopore
  - PacBio
  - BLAST
  - structural variation
  - prophage
  - phase variation
